    "https://campus.kennesaw.edu/policies-governance/handbooks/": {
      "title": "Publications and Policies",
      "description": "Publications and Policies Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Publications and Policies KSU Handbooks Welcome to the KSU Publications and Policies Portal Included on this site are links to various publications that contain policies and procedures relevant to the KSU community. The University Handbook (UH) includes information that applies to all constituencies of KSU (staff, students, faculty, administrators, vendors, members of the external community, etc.). The Employee Handbook (EH) pertains to KSU employees (i.e., anyone who receives a paycheck from KSU) while the Faculty Handbook (FH) contains policies and procedures that pertain only to faculty, and the Student Handbook (SH) contains policies and procedures that pertain to students. Links to the undergraduate and graduate catalogs are also provided as they contain\n                           some policies and procedures relevant to faculty, staff and students. University Handbook The KSU University Handbook offers a comprehensive overview of the institution's vision,\n                                             mission, and key operational policies. This resource is designed to guide faculty,\n                                             staff, and students through essential information regarding governance, advising,\n                                             services, and institutional policies. From academic program coordination to student\n                                             support services like the library, writing center, and campus wellness programs, this\n                                             publication serves as a vital tool for understanding and navigating the university's\n                                             structure and offerings. Explore this handbook to access important guidelines and resources that foster a supportive\n                                             and efficient campus environment. University Handbook Policies Faculty Handbook The Faculty Handbook serves as the official guide for faculty policies and procedures.\n                                             It outlines key information regarding institutional organization, workload expectations,\n                                             and the review and evaluation of faculty performance. Additionally, the handbook covers\n                                             personnel, fiscal, and institutional policies, providing faculty members with a clear\n                                             understanding of their responsibilities, rights, and the standards for professional\n                                             growth. Whether you're seeking information on faculty appointments, academic freedom, or performance\n                                             evaluations, this resource is essential for navigating your role here at KSU. Faculty Handbook Student Handbook The Student Handbook assists both new and returning students navigate their academic\n                                             life at Kennesaw State University. Inside, you'll find important information about\n                                             your rights, responsibilities, and the policies that guide our vibrant campus community.\n                                             We are committed to fostering a safe, inclusive, and dynamic environment for all students,\n                                             and this handbook outlines the standards we uphold together. Take time to explore its invaluable contents to make the most of your academic experience! Student Handbook Undergraduate Catalog The Undergraduate Catalog serves as the official guide to KSU's academic programs,\n                                             course offerings, and policies. Whether you're planning your course of study or working\n                                             toward graduation, the catalog is an essential resource to use alongside your academic\n                                             advisor and DegreeWorks in mapping out your next steps. Explore the catalog's features for easy navigation and advanced search options to help you find the information you need. For assistance, don’t hesitate to reach out to an academic advisor for further guidance! Undergraduate Catalog Policies Graduate Catalog The Graduate Catalog is your essential resource for navigating KSU’s graduate academic programs, courses, and updates. It is designed to support you in planning your advanced studies and ensuring you meet graduation requirements, in collaboration with your academic advisor and DegreeWorks. Use the graduate catalog for a comprehensive overview of the information needed to excel in your advanced study. The catalog features advanced search options and user-friendly navigation to help\n                                             you easily find what you need. If you have questions or need guidance on selecting\n                                             courses or degree programs, our academic advisors are here to assist you! Graduate Catalog Policies Handbook Archive & Revisions Archived University Handbooks Here, for historical purposes, are archived handbooks from previous years. 2024 - 2025 University Handbook 2023 - 2024 University Handbook 2022 - 2023 University Handbook 2021 - 2022 University Handbook (June 30, 2021) 2020 - 2021 University Handbook (June 30, 2021) 2020 - 2021 University Handbook 2019 - 2020 University Handbook 2018 - 2019 University Handbook 2017 - 2018 University Handbook Archived Faculty Handbooks Here, for historical purposes, are archived handbooks from previous years. 2024 - 2025 Faculty Handbook 2023 - 2024 Faculty Handbook (14 May 2024) 2023 - 2024 Faculty Handbook 2022 - 2023 Faculty Handbook (30 June 2023) 2022 - 2023 Faculty Handbook 2021 - 2022 Faculty Handbook (30 June 2022) 2020 - 2021 Faculty Handbook (30 June 2021) 2020 - 2021 Faculty Handbook 2019 - 2020 Faculty Handbook 2018 - 2019 Faculty Handbook 2017 - 2018 Faculty Handbook 2016 - 2017 Faculty Handbook 2015 - 2016 Faculty Handbook 2014 - 2015 Faculty Handbook 2013 - 2014 Faculty Handbook 2012 - 2013 Faculty Handbook 2011 - 2012 Faculty Handbook 2010 - 2011 Faculty Handbook 2009 - 2010 Faculty Handbook 2008 - 2009 Faculty Handbook 2007 - 2008 Faculty Handbook 2006 - 2007 Faculty Handbook 2005 - 2006 Faculty Handbook 2004 - 2005 Faculty Handbook Handbook Changelog Kennesaw State University Handbook changes from August 2025 forward. Faculty Handbook SECTION REVISION DATE REVISION DESCRIPTION REVISION TRACKING NOTES 1.1, 4.1.1, 3.12.B.2, 3.12.B.3, 3.12.B.6, 3.12.A.4, 3.12.A.5, 3.12.A.6, 3.12.B.4,\n                                                                           3.12.B.5, 3.5.A April 2, 2026 Several changes made to update the PTR process Changes Approved by shared governance in Spring 2026. 1.1 August 5, 2025 Added principal lecturers to the Corps of Instruction Added statement from BOR Policy Manual, clarifying that part-time and limited-term are not part of the Corps of Instruction Change approved by shared governance in Spring 2025. 2.13 December 1, 2025 Edited existing langauge and added additional policies for syllabus requirements and\n                                                                                 other policies. Changes approved by shared governance in Fall 2025. University Handbook Handbook Revisions Kennesaw State University Handbook changes from February  2020 - July 2025. DATE HANDBOOK SECTION DESCRIPTION 17 December 2025 Faculty 4.4.2 Minor edits and formal process clarifications. 1 July 2025 Faculty 2.8 Minor edits 27 June 2025 Faculty 4.1.2 Updates to Graduate Faculty responsibilities 24 March 2025 University 3.5 & 3.6 Updates to DFC/CFC policies 26 November 2024 University 3.1.2 Updates to standing committees 14 May 2024 Faculty 3 Updates to faculty review process 27 March 2024 Faculty 3.12.A Update to Academic Administrative Review Faculty 4.2.5 Update to Facuty and Administrative Emeritus Status and Privileges 28 March 2023 Faculty 3.13 Update to P&T schedule 10 August 2022 Faculty 3.12 Update to P&T committee election language University 3.12 Updates to list of standing committees 1 July 22 Faculty 2.9 Update regarding Grade Appeals 14 December 21 Faculty 2.9 Updated Changing Grades Section 1 July 21 Faculty 3.6 Updated section A 3.7 Updated section A 3.8 Updated section A 3.9 Updated section A 3.12 Updated the faculty review process 4.1.2 Updated affiiliate gradaute faculty status section 1 July 21 University 3.1.2 Updated standing committee information 12 May 21 Faculty 3.10 Updated to correct errors in section A 24 March 21 Faculty 4.1.2 Graduate Faculty Status section updated 1 July 20 Faculty 1.2.1 Updated to remove Enrollment Services as a support division 1.2.3 Updated Academic College information 2.1 Updated principles of Academic Freedom 3.12 Changes made to Faculty Review Process 4.4.1 Updated information regarding grants and contracts information 4.4.4 Added policy for addressing Academic Freedome Complaints University 1.1 Update to Vision and Mission 1.3 Updates to the Administrative Officers and Organization 3.1 Rules for all committees updates and updates to university bodies. 3.7.2 Updates to the curriculum review process. 4.2 Update to Writing Center text. 5.2.2 Update to Intellectual Property Policy. 5.6 Update to the Appeals policy. 24 February 20 Faculty 3.5 Updated policies on leaves and stoppoing P&T or PTR clocks. 4.2.3 Updated policies on leaves and stoppoing P&T or PTR clocks. 4.2.5 Updated policies on leaves and stoppoing P&T or PTR clocks. Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
