Z Index KSU Home Headshots for Faculty/Staff Careers Campus Community Headshots for Faculty/Staff Campus Community Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request Join us for your Headshot! Faculty and staff can now use the photobooths located in the Career Planning and Development\n                                    offices, Monday -Friday between 8:30 AM and 4:30 PM. More details are below! Class Activity/Large Group Notice Dependent on group size, taking headshots for a large party can take an extended period\n                              of time and require designated staff to assist for the duration. Please email us in\n                              advance at careerplanning@kennesaw.edu to schedule an appointment for a large group. Follow the steps below to take advantage of this free service: Visit the Department of Career Planning and Development in Kennesaw (ALC 3525) or\n                                    Marietta (Joe Mack Wilson Student Center A160). Check in with the front desk to let them know you would like to use the booth. A Student\n                                    Career Advocate or staff member will help you get started. Input your email address on the first screen (you can use your KSU email account or\n                                    a personal email account). Follow the prompts on the screen and the Iris booth will capture 3 headshot photos\n                                    at a time. Your photos will be emailed to you within minutes of the conclusion of your session. This service is available every workday from 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM! Please call ahead at 470-578-6555. Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
    "https://campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/careers/campus-community/faculty-career-champions.php": {
      "title": "Faculty Career Champions",
      "description": "Faculty Career Champions - Careers Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Faculty Career Champions Careers Campus Community Faculty Career Champions Campus Community Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request The Faculty Career Champions Program equips KSU faculty with resources, insights,\n                     and practical strategies for supporting student career development. Through a one-day\n                     training, participants explore career readiness trends, learn about key campus resources,\n                     and discover ways to integrate career readiness into their courses and student interactions.\n                     Our goal is to build a campus-wide network of faculty champions who help students\n                     prepare for their futures and make career readiness part of the KSU experience. If you're interested in becoming a Faculty Career Champion, fill out the interest\n                     form so a member of our team can follow up with you. Faculty Career Champion Interest Form Program Details Classroom Assignments FAQ Why Become a Faculty Career Champion? As a Faculty Career Champion, you'll learn about current career readiness trends and\n                           student outcomes, and gain awareness of the career resources available to your students.\n                           You'll discover practical ways to connect academics and careers, and join a network\n                           of faculty committed to student success. Along the way, you'll earn recognition as\n                           a Career Champion. What You'll Learn Career readiness competencies National and employer hiring trends Internship and experiential learning insights Career outcomes and student success data KSU career resources and referrals Strategies for embedding career readiness into coursework Benefits Professional development opportunity Recognition as a Faculty Career Champion Access to career readiness resources and materials Connection to a cross-campus network of colleagues Regular updates from the Department of Career Planning and Development Available Tools Career readiness competencies Syllabus statements Classroom activity ideas Career resource guide Employer trends reports Referral information Hear from Current Faculty Career Champions \"The workshop was a great introduction… the best part was the D2L course with assignment examples.\" \"It was a great way to bring faculty together, demonstrate what's new, and showcase\n                                 all the exceptional work that's happening at KSU regarding careers/students.\" \"It was excellent!... one of the best and most useful trainings at KSU.\" Classroom Assignments Find additional versions of these resources and more on our D2L page! Stay up to date\n                           on new developments, events, and the job fair cycle by connecting there. To be added\n                           reach out to Anthony Holmes . Career Exploration Career Fair Career-Related Event Elevator Pitch Career Foundations Badge Informational Interview LinkedIn Profile Mock Interview Resume Assignment Frequently Asked Questions Who can participate? Any Kennesaw State University faculty member may participate, regardless of rank or\n                                                   appointment type, including lecturers, assistant professors, associate professors,\n                                                   full professors, and adjunct faculty. How long is the training? The Faculty Career Champions training is approximately three hours in length. How often is training offered? The Faculty Career Champions training is offered at least twice each semester, with\n                                                   at least one session available online to provide greater flexibility and accessibility\n                                                   for faculty participants. What is expected after training? There are no formal requirements following completion of the program. Faculty Champions\n                                                   are encouraged to incorporate what they learn into their courses and interactions\n                                                   with students, utilize career readiness resources, and help connect students with\n                                                   relevant opportunities and support services when appropriate. Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
    "https://campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/careers/campus-community/hiring-students.php": {
      "title": "Hiring Student and Staff Workers",
      "description": "Hiring Student and Staff Workers - Careers Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Hiring Student and Staff Workers Careers Campus Community Hiring Student and Staff Workers Campus Community Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request Hiring Student, Interns and Staff Workers Hiring a student worker now takes place in Handshake, KSU’s Career Management System. Students rely on Handshake for finding all types of jobs including student assistant positions, Federal Work-Study (FWS) , graduate assistant positions, and internship positions. Note: all FWS positions posted in Handshake will be reviewed and approved by the Financial\n                     Aid office ( fws@kennesaw.edu ). While the front end of the hiring process will take place in Handshake, hiring managers\n                     will continue to work with Human Resources to onboard new student employees, select\n                     start dates, and to ensure they will be paid. We’ve outlined the steps below: Register in Handshake as an “Employer” contact with Kennesaw State University. If you have a student account, use steps to Create an Employer Account Linked to Your Student Account. Having trouble? Contact us at careerplanning@kennesaw.edu or 470-578-6555 . Once registered, you will be approved by us to post your positions. Unwanted notifications? Customize your notification preferences . To create a dept. name as a Division within KSU (ex. Sports and Recreation, Criminal\n                                    Justice Dept., ESSM.) email sgoodm23@kennesaw.edu with the dept. name, abbreviation, or acronym. You are now ready to post jobs in Handshake ! For a faster student application choose Apply through external system and attach a\n                                    URL of your office application. This will bypass students' resume approval by Career\n                                    Planning and Development. Run your interview and selection process with the candidates who have applied to your\n                              position in Handshake (feel free to encourage students to apply to your posting by\n                              sharing the link to your position). Once you have selected the student(s) you'd like to hire, please complete the SEHF\n                              form and send it to Human Resources at hr@kennesaw.edu . Wait for confirmation from Human Resources, and messaging about the onboarding process. Send \"thank you for applying\" Handshake messages or emails to all applicants not hired. For more information about student employment at KSU (including the hiring process\n                                    through HR, pay structure, and using OneUSG), please visit https://campus.kennesaw.edu/faculty-staff/human-resources/student-employment/. If you need additional assistance, please contact our office. We've also provided\n                           some resources and tips below to help you make the most of your experience working\n                           with student employees. Important Resources Creating a Learning Environment for Effective Supervision For any additional assistance, please don't hesitate to contact our office. Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
    "https://campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/careers/campus-community/learning-environment.php": {
      "title": "Learning Environment",
      "description": "Learning Environment - Careers Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Learning Environment Careers Campus Community Learning Environment Campus Community Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request Hiring and Creating a Learning Environment for Student Workers Establish clear goals. Provide training, performance expectations, and set ground rules. Develop a student\n                        employee manual. Delegate! Assume that the students you have hired are competent and responsible. Provide them\n                        with the potential for learning and growth. Set a positive example of professional, polite, and ethical behavior . If students witness a supervisor that is punctual and professional, students will\n                        learn to do the same. Remember that student employees are students first. If there is a conflict between a student's academics and job, academics must come\n                        first. The student can and should however learn how to manage time so that the impact\n                        on the position is minimal. Make it clear what is expected regarding the commitment\n                        and how to notify you if they must be absent. Show appreciation for exceptional work . Positive feedback, especially when given in front of one's peers, costs nothing\n                        and provides a quick, effective reward. Allow for student input . Ask your student employees what they think of a certain project. They have a lot\n                        to offer! Be an accessible supervisor . Tell students they are free to ask you questions and discuss concerns. Periodically\n                        ask them if they have any questions. Be a student . Learn how to improve your skills. Attend workshops, take classes, and read. Be a teacher. You most likely possess a great deal of knowledge and skills, so share these with\n                        your employees. Encourage risk-taking and decision-making . Letting students know that you trust as well as believe in them helps to foster\n                        a sense of cohesiveness, which can lead to increased self-esteem. Please remember\n                        that this is a learning experience for the students you hire. Communicate openly and honestly . A student should always know how they are doing. Help students understand the value of their position . Student jobs can and should be centered around learning, and preparing students\n                        for future jobs. Be sure to help students understand what is transferable from their\n                        student job into future jobs they may hold. RETURN TO HIRING INSTRUCTIONS PAGE Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
    "https://campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/careers/campus-community/micro-credentials.php": {
      "title": "Micro-Credentials",
      "description": "Micro-Credentials - Careers Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Micro-Credentials Careers Campus Community Micro-Credentials Campus Community Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request Overview Micro-credentials are digital records of a learner’s successful completion of educational activities that lead to professional skills and competencies that are not reflected on a transcript. In many cases, these digital records include archives (metadata) of the work that led to the award. While transcript-based records are restricted to the final results of for-credit classes and programs of study, micro-credentials can be granted for any kind of learning initiative. KSU students, faculty and staff who engage in micro-credential programs will be able\n                        to trumpet their development at KSU in meaningful ways. KSU faculty and unit leaders will be able to highlight career-focused elements of\n                        their courses, training programs, and extracurricular activities (career prep, speaker\n                        series, international, etc.), connecting in-classroom learning with real-world credentials. KSU Administration will have a convenient tool for measuring engagement. KSU uses Badgr as the micro-credential host. Micro-Credential Examples Skills can increase a micro-credential’s value in the job market by conveying the job skills it represents. Each skill affiliated will link to related job information in the micro-credential’s Badgr page. Skills for Ribbons, Badges, & Digital Certificates should be identified in partnership with the Department of Career Planning & Development. Micro-Credentials should be rooted in industry/professional standards, the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies or other valued job skills. (NACE) Career Readiness Competencies Micro-Credential Proposal Process Visit the Curriculum, Instruction, and Assessment site for more information on submitting\n                           a proposal for a micro-credential. Micro-Credentials Overview Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
    "https://campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/careers/campus-community/presentation-request.php": {
      "title": "Presentation Request",
      "description": "Presentation Request - Careers Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Presentation Request Careers Campus Community Presentation Request Campus Community Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request Staff from the Department of Career Planning & Development (DCPD) are available to support KSU classes, programs, and events in a variety of ways—from brief classroom visits to active participation at campus events. Use the options below to request the type of support that best fits your needs. For the best chance of ensuring staff availability, please submit all requests at least two weeks in advance. Please note: you will need to be signed in with your KSU login to access the form. Request a Classroom or Group Presentation DCPD advisors are available to present to your class or group for as little as five\n                                    minutes or up to an hour (or more). Presentation topics include: An overview of DCPD services and resources How to participate in internships or co-ops “How-to” sessions on resume writing, interviewing, and job fair preparation We can also connect your class or group with employers interested in engaging with\n                                       students. Note: If you will not be present for class, it is your responsibility to secure room access\n                                    for the presenter. Submit a Presentation Request Have Us Attend Your Event as a Resource DCPD staff can also support campus events in ways that go beyond traditional presentations. We’re happy to attend your event as a resource and can serve as: Tabling representatives Event speakers or panelists Resume reviewers Career-focused resources for students Other similar support roles aligned with your event goals We can be present and on deck to help expose students to career-ready skills, guidance,\n                                    and connections that support their future success. Submit an Event Resource Request Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
