      "description": "Careers - Human Resources Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer KSU Home Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government A-Z Index KSU Home Careers Human Resources Careers Careers Home Talent Acquisition Background Checks Frequently Asked Questions Find My Recruiter Interviewing KSU Community Position Approval Process Registered Visitors Staff Hiring Process Human Resources Careers at KSU Welcome to KSU’s online job site.  The online applicant system provides you with the ability to review job opportunities and apply to those that you are interested in and feel qualified for.  Each job posting has a summary description of the position and required qualifications. All job applications must be submitted through the online system. Application stations are available in the Office of Human Resources for anyone needing assistance to apply. Requirements for employment can be found here. Internal Faculty and Staff Log into OneUSG Connect >> Click the Recruiting Self Service tile >> Then, click the\n                                       Apply for Jobs tile. External Applicants Click here to view faculty and staff job opportunities >> View all jobs >> Filter\n                                       or search by job details. Student Assistant Jobs Current students may click here to view posted opportunities >> Half-time enrollment\n                                       required. Professional Education Openings Click here for more details about specific instructional opportunities. Benefits at a Glance! Download this page to preview the perks available at KSU! Why KSU? At KSU, you can find your place, your rhythm, and your calling. Experience the passion of being an Owl! Take a virtual tour of KSU today! Interested in becoming faculty or staff at Kennesaw State? Follow these easy steps below! STEP 1: SEARCHING AND APPLYING FOR A JOB Begin your job search by reviewing our current postings until you find the one in which you’re interested. Next, click “Apply” and complete the online application.  You've successfully completed the job submission process for the position you selected when you reach the “Thank You” page. STEP 2: INTERVIEWING Use this opportunity to tell us more about your skills and we will share more about\n                                          the job opportunity, our department and the culture at KSU. You should expect a series\n                                          of one-on-one interviews. However, some positions may require a panel interview in\n                                          which several people will ask you questions. STEP 3: EMPLOYMENT SCREENING If you are extended an offer and choose to accept, we will conduct a thorough pre-employment\n                                          screening. This screening may include, but is not limited to, verifying your work\n                                          and education history, a criminal background investigation, and a drug test. STEP 4: HIRING Congratulations. You have now successfully completed the hiring process. Your next\n                                          step is to complete the New Employee Orientation and report to your first day of work!\n                                          While this may be the last step in the hiring process, we anticipate it being your\n                                          first step toward fulfilling your career potential as a KSU owl. Kennesaw State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer.\n                           It is the policy of Kennesaw State University to recruit, hire, train, promote and\n                           educate persons without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, national\n                           origin race religion, sexual orientation, or status as a protected Veteran. Kennesaw State University is a participant in the Employment Eligibility Verification Program (E-Verify) effective October 15, 2007.  Participant ID: 61415 Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only ©"
    },
