    "https://assistive.usablenet.com/tt/campus.kennesaw.edu/offices-services/careers/campus-community/faculty-career-champions.php": {
      "title": "Faculty Career Champions",
      "description": "Faculty Career Champions - Careers https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-M5WN4MT Skip to main navigation Skip to main content Skip to footer Kennesaw State University KSU Home Arrow Navigate Icon Current Students MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express KSUmail DegreeWorks KCash Owl Life Handshake Course Evaluations Campus Services Dining Parking & Transportation University Libraries Student Health Services Service Portal Student Employment Campus Directory Academic Resources Tutoring Resources Student Success Advising Student Handbook Bursar Financial Aid University Registrar Faculty & Staff MyKSU Resources D2L Brightspace Owl Express/Banner KSUmail KSU Connect VPN Academic Resources Academic Affairs Faculty Affairs Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning Course Evaluations Open Education Resources Faculty Handbook Promotion & Tenure University Registrar Employee Resources Service Portal Human Resources Campus Services University Information Technology Services Campus Directory Payroll OneUSG Connect Colleges Colleges Coles College of Business Geer College of the Arts College of Architecture & Construction Management Bagwell College of Education College of Computing & Software Engineering Norman J. Radow College of Humanities & Social Sciences College of Science & Mathematics Graduate College KSU Journey Honors College Southern Polytechnic College of Engineering & Engineering Technology Wellstar College of Health & Human Services KSU Kennesaw Campus, Kennesaw Hall building. Offices & Services Offices & Services University Registrar Parking & Transportation Student Affairs Housing & Residence Life Event & Venue Management University Information Technology Services Fiscal Services University Libraries Academic Advising Campus Operations Strategic Communications & Marketing Students walk across a crosswalk near the Academic Learning Center at Kennesaw State University Policies & Governance Policy Resources University Handbooks Institutional Policies Complaints & Appeals Conflict of Interest General Data Protection Regulation Protecting Minors Public Forum FERPA Governance University Council Administrators Council Staff Senate Faculty Senate Student Government KSU Kennesaw Campus, Kennesaw Hall building A-Z Index KSU Home Arrow Navigate Icon Magnifying Glass Icon Close Menu Icon magnifying glass Open Menu Icon Close Menu Icon Faculty Career Champions Faculty Career Champions Careers Campus Community Faculty Career Champions Campus Community Chevron Down Icon Alumni Account Headshots for Faculty/Staff Faculty Career Champions Hiring Students and Interns Learning Environment and Effective Supervision Micro-Credentials Presentation Request The Faculty Career Champions Program equips KSU faculty with resources, insights, and practical strategies for supporting student career development. Through a one-day training, participants explore career readiness trends, learn about key campus resources, and discover ways to integrate career readiness into their courses and student interactions. Our goal is to build a campus-wide network of faculty champions who help students prepare for their futures and make career readiness part of the KSU experience. If you're interested in becoming a Faculty Career Champion, fill out the interest form so a member of our team can follow up with you. Faculty Career Champion Interest Form Program Details Classroom Assignments FAQ Why Become a Faculty Career Champion? As a Faculty Career Champion, you'll learn about current career readiness trends and student outcomes, and gain awareness of the career resources available to your students. You'll discover practical ways to connect academics and careers, and join a network of faculty committed to student success. Along the way, you'll earn recognition as a Career Champion. What You'll Learn Career readiness competencies National and employer hiring trends Internship and experiential learning insights Career outcomes and student success data KSU career resources and referrals Strategies for embedding career readiness into coursework Benefits Professional development opportunity Recognition as a Faculty Career Champion Access to career readiness resources and materials Connection to a cross-campus network of colleagues Regular updates from the Department of Career Planning and Development Available Tools Career readiness competencies Syllabus statements Classroom activity ideas Career resource guide Employer trends reports Referral information Hear from Current Faculty Career Champions \"The workshop was a great introduction… the best part was the D2L course with assignment examples.\" \"It was a great way to bring faculty together, demonstrate what's new, and showcase all the exceptional work that's happening at KSU regarding careers/students.\" \"It was excellent!... one of the best and most useful trainings at KSU.\" Classroom Assignments Find additional versions of these resources and more on our D2L page! Stay up to date on new developments, events, and the job fair cycle by connecting there. To be added reach out to Anthony Holmes . Career Exploration Career Fair Career-Related Event Elevator Pitch Career Foundations Badge Informational Interview LinkedIn Profile Mock Interview Resume Assignment Frequently Asked Questions Who can participate? Any Kennesaw State University faculty member may participate, regardless of rank or appointment type, including lecturers, assistant professors, associate professors, full professors, and adjunct faculty. How long is the training? The Faculty Career Champions training is approximately three hours in length. How often is training offered? The Faculty Career Champions training is offered at least twice each semester, with at least one session available online to provide greater flexibility and accessibility for faculty participants. What is expected after training? There are no formal requirements following completion of the program. Faculty Champions are encouraged to incorporate what they learn into their courses and interactions with students, utilize career readiness resources, and help connect students with relevant opportunities and support services when appropriate. Kennesaw State University Logo Facebook Icon X Icon LinkedIn Icon Instagram Icon YouTube Icon Contact Information Kennesaw Campus 1000 Chastain Road Kennesaw, GA 30144 Marietta Campus 1100 South Marietta Pkwy Marietta, GA 30060 Phone 470-KSU-INFO (470-578-4636) Campus Maps Parking Media Resources Campus A-Z Index Academic Calendar Campus News D2L Brightspace University Information Technology Services Related Links Libraries Housing Financial Aid Degrees, Majors & Programs Registrar Job Opportunities Campus Security Global Education Sustainability Accessibility © 2026 Kennesaw State University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Statement Accreditation Advisories Report a Concern Feedback Open Records Human Trafficking Notice Text Only © Top of page Assistive Options Change the current font size: larger | default | smaller Current color mode is Black on White , other available mode: Yellow on Black Show textual links as buttons Do not move navbars Do not alert me when leaving dynamic conforming version Open not handled documents directly Hide Assistive Options Open the original version of this page. UsableNet Assistive is a UsableNet product. UsableNet Assistive Main Page ."
    }
